# 6. Bug Reports

## Definition

A Bug Report is a formal document used by QA Engineers to communicate defects to the development team.

---

## Purpose

A Bug Report helps developers:

- Understand the issue.
- Reproduce the defect.
- Investigate efficiently.
- Fix the defect.
- Reduce investigation time.

---

## Contents of a Bug Report

- Bug ID
- Title
- Environment
- Preconditions
- Steps to Reproduce
- Expected Result
- Actual Result
- Severity
- Priority
- Attachments
- Reporter
- Status

---

## Characteristics of a Good Bug Report

A Bug Report should be:

- Clear
- Complete
- Accurate
- Professional
- Reproducible

---

## Interview Tip

The most important part of a Bug Report is writing clear and complete **Steps to Reproduce**, because developers should be able to reproduce the defect without asking additional questions.

---

# 7. Test Plan

## Definition

A Test Plan is a project-level document that defines how testing will be performed for a specific project.

---

## Purpose

A Test Plan helps:

- Define testing scope.
- Plan resources.
- Assign responsibilities.
- Define timelines.
- Identify risks.
- Organize testing activities.

---

## Prepared By

Usually prepared by:

- QA Lead
- Test Lead
- QA Manager

---

## Remember

A Test Plan is created separately for every project.

---

# 8. Test Strategy

## Definition

A Test Strategy is an organization-level document that defines the overall testing approach and standards followed across multiple projects.

---

## Purpose

A Test Strategy helps:

- Standardize testing.
- Maintain consistency.
- Define testing standards.
- Improve quality across projects.

---

## Prepared By

Usually prepared by:

- QA Manager
- Test Manager

---

## Test Strategy vs Test Plan

| Test Strategy | Test Plan |
|---------------|-----------|
| Organization level | Project level |
| Reused across projects | Created for each project |
| Defines standards | Defines execution plan |
| Long-term | Project-specific |

